# core/data/talk/grammar/en/core_bulk_k.tlk - bulk Surface push K: replies to a telling and to an
# opinion, each rule's name matches its act table row (owner: TK; T5b). Clean in any room: no
# register word, no romance, no cool act, no guard change. Rule names end in _uk. Syntax:
# core/tools/talkc_gen.py.

@rule core.tell.uk1 act: backchannel
  "Oh, that's interesting. Tell me the rest of it."
  "Mm, I didn't know that. Go on, I'm listening."
  "Huh. Right. That's a new one for me."
  "I see. Keep going, I want the whole story."
  "Okay, I'm following. What happened after that?"
  "Hm, that sounds like a lot. How did you manage?"
  "Wow. You've been busy. Tell me more when you can."
  "Right, I'd not heard that before. Thanks for sharing."
  "Oh? That's a surprise. I'm all ears."
  "Interesting, go on. I'll try not to interrupt."
@rule core.tell.uk2 act: ask_about
  "Wait, what did they say when you told them?"
  "And did it turn out the way you hoped?"
  "Where did you hear that, if you don't mind me asking?"
  "How did you feel about it at the time?"
  "Was it the first time that happened, or has it happened before?"
  "What was the best part of that, for you?"
  "Did anyone else get involved, or was it just you?"
  "What would you do differently, looking back on it?"
  "Who was there with you when all that happened?"
  "How long did that take, all told?"
@rule core.tell.uk3 act: opine_pos
  "That sounds like a good time, honestly. I'd have loved it."
  "I think you handled that really well. Good for you."
  "What a lovely thing to have happen. I'm happy for you."
  "I'd call that a win, even if it felt small at the time."
  "That's the kind of story I'd like to hear again."
  "You made that sound fun. I'm jealous, a bit."
  "I like how that turned out. Nicely done, you."
  "That was a good call. I'd have done the same, probably."
@rule core.tell.uk4 act: opine_neg
  "That sounds awful. I'm sorry it went that way."
  "Oof, I'd have hated that too. Who does that?"
  "That's not fair. You deserved a better outcome."
  "I'm not surprised it bothered you. It would bother me."
  "That's a rough one. I hope the rest of the week is kinder."
  "Honestly, that's a bit much. I'd be annoyed too."
  "Ugh, that's the sort of thing that sticks with you."
  "That's a pity. Things should have gone the other way."
@rule core.tell.uk5 act: joke
  "Plot twist. I'd have fainted and then asked for a sandwich."
  "I'd have needed a nap, a snack and a very long sit down."
  "Wow, that's a lot of drama for one afternoon, isn't it?"
  "Next time, try telling it in fewer chapters. Thanks."
  "Great story. Needs a better ending, and maybe a cat."
@rule core.tell.uk6 act: laugh
  "Ha! I can't believe that actually happened to you."
  "Hee, that's the best thing I've heard all day."
  "Ha, okay, that was a whole production. Well done."
@rule core.tell.uk7 act: tease
  "You always have the best stories, somehow. Show-off."
  "Look at you, holding court with a story like that."
  "Honestly, you could do stand-up with that material."
@rule core.opine_pos.uk1 act: agree
  "Yes! I'm glad we both think it's good, it's rare."
  "You're right, it's a good one. We have excellent taste."
  "Totally agree. It's the best part of the whole day."
  "Exactly. I'd say the same, and I'd say it loudly."
  "Right, it's great. I'm glad you noticed it too."
@rule core.opine_pos.uk2 act: disagree
  "I'm not sure about that. It was nice, but not perfect."
  "Hm, I'd call it good, but not quite great, sorry."
  "I see why you like it. I just don't feel it as much."
@rule core.opine_pos.uk3 act: opine_neg
  "I love it, but I'll admit it has a few rough edges."
  "It's good, yes, though I'd change the last bit a little."
@rule core.opine_pos.uk4 act: laugh
  "Ha! You really love it, huh? It shows on your face."
  "Hee, you sound so sure about it. I like that."
@rule core.opine_neg.uk1 act: agree
  "Yes, that's the truth. It's a bit of a mess, really."
  "Right? I'd put it in the bin and start again."
  "Exactly. You put it better than I would have."
  "Agreed, that one's not for me either. Good call."
@rule core.opine_neg.uk2 act: disagree
  "Hm, I don't think it's that bad. A bit slow, maybe."
  "I'd give it another go. It grows on you, sometimes."
  "I see your point, though I'd be a bit kinder to it."
@rule core.opine_neg.uk3 act: sympathize
  "Oh no, that sounds really frustrating. I'm sorry."
  "That's a hard feeling to shake off. I get it."
  "I'm sorry it went that way. It's not fun to sit through."
@rule core.opine_neg.uk4 act: tease
  "Wow, so harsh. Did it do something to you personally?"
  "Strong words, friend. What did it ever do to you?"
@rule core.opine_neg.uk5 act: joke
  "I'd put it on the list of things we don't talk about."
  "Well, it's not winning any popularity contests today."
